  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 126 AM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nAnother hot day across the area on Thursday. However both the GFS \nand Euro are now showing a stronger wave moving through the Plains \non Thursday night and Friday. The GFS being the stronger of the two \nmodels, which might suppress the ridge sufficiently for a front to \nmove into the area along with perhaps some precip chances Friday \ninto Saturday. The Euro is more reserved and keeps the precip to our \nnorth and east, so we will not get overly excited about this \nprospect yet, but it is something to watch. The latest NBM is \nintroducing some low pops for late Friday. However, the better bet \nis for a few degrees of cooling, otherwise, the heat will continue \nthrough the end of the week and the upcoming weekend. \n\nI guess one thing to watch is the gulf as a possible tropical system \ntakes shape over the next couple of days. Currently is does not \nappear that this system will have any direct impact on Oklahoma or \nnorth Texas as the upper high keeps the system well to our south \nacross south Texas into northern Mexico.",
